problems.problem:
Claire and Stuart play a game called Nifty Nines:
(i) they take turns to choose one number at a time, with Claire choosing first;
(ii) numbers can only be chosen from the integers $1$ to $5$ inclusive;
(iii) the game ends when $n$ numbers have been chosen (repetitions are permitted).
Stuart wins the game if the sum of the chosen numbers is a multiple of $9$, otherwise Claire wins.
Find all values of $n$ for which Claire can ensure a win, whatever Stuart's choices were. You must prove that you have found them all.
